comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T14:35:55.235Z",codex-agent,"Saved-WIP comparison: all four source changes and their artifact-state regressions already landed through PR #191 (d1087cf). No source hunks remain to reapply. Copying the WIP would remove later seed normalization and artifact ownership. Keep main source intact, add focused independent black-box regression coverage and mutation proofs, rebuild dist and run npm/Bun release gates. PR #203 remains open; its implementation, tests and tracker items are excluded. The generated changelog will be refreshed as required after final tracker writes."
  "2026-11-07T14:39:15.993Z",codex-agent,"Focused acceptance passes 4/4 with zero failures or skips. Reproducible disposable-copy revert verifier passes baseline 4/4; kills seven isolated mutations (binding alias, template alias, seed alias, ownership record alias, catalog guard removal, replacement privacy guard removal, sensitive seed-prefix guard removal); all seven restored scenarios pass. No production source was altered: these certify behaviors already delivered by PR #191. Every fixture is synthetic and uses real nongit SDK trackers."
  "2026-11-07T14:45:58.225Z",codex-agent,"Expanded the disposable verifier with a settings-alias mutation: baseline 4/4, now 8/8 independent behavioral reverts fail with assertions and all 8 restorations pass. npm typecheck, lint, build:test and docstrings pass (95 files, 227 declarations). Both linked pm tests passed with result tracking disabled as required; no run artifacts were written to the package tracker. Isolated strict health passes; ordinary host health reports the existing global pm-github version skew. Current source, rebuilt dist and generated CHANGELOG are byte-identical to main; no paths owned by open PR #203 are changed."
  "2026-11-07T14:57:46.146Z",codex-agent,"Final local gates pass on unchanged source at unchanged thresholds: npm run release:check 348/348 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, test duration 418812 ms; bun run release:check 348/348 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Both report 100.00% lines/branches/functions across all 36 required source files. Typecheck, lint, docstrings (95 files and 227 declarations), test compilation, production audit, package inspection, changelog and both release verifiers pass. Focused suite passes 4/4. Linked disposable verifier now passes all 8 isolated revert proofs and all 8 restorations. Source, rebuilt dist and generated changelog are identical to main. Only this new issue, its history, focused tests, verifier and verification notes are changed. No saved source/test hunk remains to port because PR #191 already delivered them; saved dist and closed-feature tracker edits are dropped. No merge, package release or bot trigger performed. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; CI will start when the single follow-up PR opens. Existing global extension/host version skew remains outside scope; isolated strict tracker health passes."
  "2026-11-07T15:19:57.855Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: both CodeRabbit findings are valid instances of the same evidence rule: successful exit or an arbitrary assertion token does not prove the required named tests executed with the required verdict. Inspect baseline, each behavioral mutation, and restoration as named test outcomes; reject missing, skipped, todo, cancelled, duplicate or unexpected tests and failures from the wrong origin. Audit package-wide reporting and mutation helpers, add adversarial regression coverage, retain the eight original behavioral proofs, then run focused and full npm/Bun gates. Main is not ahead of this PR (one branch commit, zero main-only commits); no merge is needed."
  "2026-11-07T15:28:51.006Z",codex-agent,"Class audit complete: the exit-only baseline/restoration and whole-output assertion-token check were confined to tests/fixtures/typed-binding-revert.ts. All three phases now use assertNamedResults over terminal Node reporter events: four exact unique names, no skipped/todo/cancelled/missing/extra/nested tests, and the designated mutation test must fail with its own ERR_ASSERTION cause while all other tests pass. Counts are emitted only after validation. Audited scripts/coverage-gate.ts, scripts/sdk-seed-differential.ts, public validation scripts, SDK fixture commands, and npm/Bun packed JSON/TOON and nongit consumers: their data assertions/counts are explicit; no equivalent unchecked named-test claim found. No production command/output or protected PR #203 file changes are needed. Focused acceptance and adversarial evidence tests pass 8/8. Added tests exercise the actual verifier entrypoint as well as structured evidence, including empty runs, missing/skipped/todo tests at every slot, cancellation, filtering, duplicate/unknown names, misleading stdout, wrong failure origin and skipped restoration. The eight original typed-binding behavioral reverts remain detected and all restorations pass."
  "2026-11-07T15:30:53.476Z",codex-agent,"Review regression proofs in a disposable package copy: all 6 isolated behavioral reverts fail the intended adversarial test and all 6 restorations pass. Reverts: baseline status-only reporting, mutation status-only attribution, restoration status-only acceptance, removed exact-inventory guard, removed skipped-result guard, and removed target assertion-cause guard. Commands were node --test --test-concurrency=2 with test-name-pattern selecting the actual-verifier, malformed-record or mutation-evidence regression in tests/revert-evidence.test.ts. The actual-verifier regression detects false baseline reports, a failure in the wrong named test, and a skipped restoration before any success message. No reviewed checkout source was mutated. Typecheck, lint and test compilation pass; docstrings cover 97 files and 232 declarations. Source, rebuilt dist, package configuration and changelog remain identical to main."
  "2026-11-07T15:39:34.605Z",codex-agent,"Broader numeric-summary audit extends the named-test audit: scripts/sdk-seed-differential.ts also hard-coded 14 matching observations, and scripts/validate-plan-public.ts hard-coded 7 backend pairs. Both now count only completed assertions. Property tests execute the actual reporting blocks across empty, small, current and expanded inventories, multiple snapshots and failed comparisons. Real SDK contracts and a synthetic nongit tracker verify planning counts and unchanged tracker bytes; no SDK mocks or original-data chmod operations. New count tests pass 3/3. The four evidence-regression tests also pass on the minimum supported Node 22.18.0 and Node 26.13.0 (4/4 each), validating reporter compatibility."
  "2026-11-07T15:40:27.224Z",codex-agent,"Numeric-count revert proofs pass in disposable copies: restoring literal 14 in the differential snapshot report fails the cardinality property, and restoring literal 7 in the plan pair report fails the real-SDK nongit subset property. Both fixed restorations pass 3/3. Combined with six named-result/attribution reverts, this review round has 8/8 detected behavioral reverts and 8/8 passing restorations; the original eight typed-binding reverts also pass through linked pm test. Linked focused tests pass 8/8, linked count tests pass 3/3; no test-run artifacts are recorded. Starting both full release gates at unchanged thresholds with at most two workers."
  "2026-11-07T16:13:54.802Z",codex-agent,"Review-round final validation: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass 355/355 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100.00% lines/branches/functions across all 36 gated source files at unchanged thresholds. Test durations: npm 1132331 ms; Bun 743678 ms. Typecheck, lint, test compilation, docstrings (98 files, 233 declarations), production audit, package inspection, changelog and release verifiers pass. Focused linked checks pass 8/8 plus count properties 3/3; evidence/count tests pass 7/7 on Node 22.18.0 and 26.13.0. Eight review-specific reverts and eight original typed-binding reverts are detected, with all restorations passing. Both CodeRabbit findings are fixed across baseline, mutation and restoration evidence, plus the two related numeric validation reports. No original test was weakened or deleted. Production src, rebuilt dist, package configuration and protected PR #203 files are unchanged. Follow-up PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/205 . After pushing, answer the review-body finding, resolve the verified inline finding and request the newly authorized CodeRabbit re-review. CI/re-review on the final pushed head is not yet claimed. Leave item in_progress for orchestrator verification and release this claim."
